  "live_records": {
    "q-75203": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75203",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t}⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$",
      "worked_solution": "At the point where $t=0$,  the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{0},\\,{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,\\,{e}^{0},\\,-{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point \n where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩+u⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75203-a",
